# Flamebox Fast-Food — Supabase Setup & SQL Schema

Follow these instructions to link your Supabase database with Flamebox and enable real-time synchronization for products, menu items, orders, and store settings.

---

## 1. Environment Credentials

Make sure your `.env` file in the project root contains your Supabase credentials:

```env
# Supabase Configuration (Get these from your NEW Supabase project settings -> API)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=<YOUR_NEW_SUPABASE_URL>
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<YOUR_NEW_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY>

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=<YOUR_NEW_SUPABASE_URL>
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<YOUR_NEW_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY>
```

---

## 2. SQL Code to Run in Supabase SQL Editor

Go to your **Supabase Dashboard** -> **SQL Editor** -> **New Query**, paste the SQL code below, and click **Run**.

```sql
-- ==========================================
-- 1. DROP EXISTING TABLES IF EXISTS (CLEAN SLATE)
-- ==========================================
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS on_auth_user_created ON auth.users;
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS public.handle_new_user();
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS public.profiles CASCADE;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS public.orders CASCADE;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS public.menu_items CASCADE;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS public.categories CASCADE;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS public.store_settings CASCADE;

-- ==========================================
-- 2. CREATE PROFILES TABLE & AUTH TRIGGER
-- ==========================================
CREATE TABLE public.profiles (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    full_name TEXT,
    email TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    phone TEXT,
    address TEXT,
    is_admin BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()
);

ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "Public profiles are viewable by everyone." ON public.profiles FOR SELECT USING (true);
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert their own profile." ON public.profiles FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = id);
CREATE POLICY "Users can update own profile." ON public.profiles FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = id);

-- Trigger to automatically create a profile for each new user
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN
  INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, full_name, email)
  VALUES (new.id, new.raw_user_meta_data->>'full_name', new.email);
  RETURN new;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER;

CREATE TRIGGER on_auth_user_created
  AFTER INSERT ON auth.users
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE PROCEDURE public.handle_new_user();

-- ==========================================
-- 3. CREATE MENU ITEMS TABLE
-- ==========================================
CREATE TABLE public.menu_items (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    description TEXT,
    price NUMERIC(10, 2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.00,
    image TEXT,
    category TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Burgers',
    rating NUMERIC(3, 1) DEFAULT 4.8,
    bestseller BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
    spicy BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
    veg BOOLEAN DEFAULT false,
    in_stock BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- Enable RLS & Allow Public Access
ALTER TABLE public.menu_items ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "Public Read Access Menu" ON public.menu_items FOR SELECT USING (true);
CREATE POLICY "Public Insert Access Menu" ON public.menu_items FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (true);
CREATE POLICY "Public Update Access Menu" ON public.menu_items FOR UPDATE USING (true);
CREATE POLICY "Public Delete Access Menu" ON public.menu_items FOR DELETE USING (true);

-- ==========================================
-- 3. CREATE ORDERS TABLE
-- ==========================================
CREATE TABLE public.orders (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    customer JSONB NOT NULL,
    items JSONB NOT NULL,
    payment_method TEXT DEFAULT 'card',
    subtotal NUMERIC(10, 2) DEFAULT 0.00,
    delivery NUMERIC(10, 2) DEFAULT 2.99,
    tax NUMERIC(10, 2) DEFAULT 0.00,
    total NUMERIC(10, 2) DEFAULT 0.00,
    status TEXT DEFAULT 'Pending',
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()
);

ALTER TABLE public.orders ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "Public Access Orders" ON public.orders FOR ALL USING (true);

-- ==========================================
-- 4. INSERT DEFAULT MENU ITEMS
-- ==========================================
INSERT INTO public.menu_items (id, name, description, price, image, category, rating, bestseller, spicy, veg, in_stock) VALUES
('1', 'Classic Cheeseburger', 'Juicy beef patty, cheddar, fresh lettuce & tomato.', 8.99, '/assets/food-burger.jpg', 'Burgers', 4.8, true, false, false, true),
('2', 'Double Bacon Stack', 'Two patties, crispy bacon, molten cheddar.', 12.50, '/assets/food-burger2.jpg', 'Burgers', 4.9, true, false, false, true),
('3', 'Pepperoni Pizza', 'Wood-fired crust, mozzarella, spicy pepperoni.', 14.00, '/assets/food-pizza.jpg', 'Pizza', 4.7, true, true, false, true),
('4', 'Golden Fries', 'Hand-cut, sea-salted, crispy perfection.', 3.99, '/assets/food-fries.jpg', 'Sides', 4.6, false, false, true, true),
('5', 'Loaded Nachos', 'Melted cheese, jalapeños, salsa & sour cream.', 7.50, '/assets/food-nachos.jpg', 'Sides', 4.5, false, true, true, true),
('6', 'Buffalo Wings', 'Crispy wings tossed in fiery hot sauce.', 9.99, '/assets/food-wings.jpg', 'Sides', 4.8, true, true, false, true),
('7', 'Iced Cola', 'Ice-cold refreshing classic cola.', 2.50, '/assets/food-drink.jpg', 'Beverages', 4.4, false, false, true, true),
('8', 'Molten Lava Cake', 'Warm chocolate cake with vanilla ice cream.', 5.99, '/assets/food-dessert.jpg', 'Desserts', 4.9, true, false, true, true)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
```

---

## 3. Realtime Enablement (Optional)

If you want real-time updates across multiple open browser tabs:
1. In Supabase Dashboard, navigate to **Database** -> **Publications**.
2. Click `supabase_realtime` and enable replication for `menu_items` and `orders`.
